   "description": "Mount Everest, Sagarmatha in Nepali and Chomolungma in Tibetan, is the highest mountain on Earth. Edmund Hillary and Tenzing Norgay first reached the summit on 29 May 1953 by the South Col route from Nepal.\n\nThe route climbs the Khumbu Icefall, the Western Cwm and the Lhotse Face to the South Col, then follows the Southeast Ridge over the South Summit and the Hillary Step to the top."
